# __PROJECT_NAME__ agent guide

AGENTS.md is a symlink to this file. Keep code, documentation, comments and agent instructions in English.
Read .agents/skills/project/SKILL.md and node_modules/@arbol-ai/maximus/skills/maximus/SKILL.md.

## Structure

This is an API-first Maximus project. vite.config.ts is its only configuration: maximus() states the
application and its Worker, and errors.ts, context.ts and auth.ts complete it in code.
Each route file default-exports defineHandler(handler, contract): routes/v1/tasks/[taskId].delete.ts answers
DELETE /api/v1/tasks/{taskId}. Declare strict schemas; the name, effect and scope derive from the method
and path unless declared. MCP and RPC exposure use the same contracts; mcp/tools/ holds MCP-only tools.
The Vite plugin and maximus prepare reconcile generated .maximus/ entries before builds. Never edit them.
src/ is optional shared domain code. Root modules never import generated modules or routes.
Middleware files are ordered by name: defineMiddleware wraps HTTP before token admission and has no
principal; defineOperationMiddleware runs after native admission across HTTP, MCP and RPC. Middleware
imports configuration types only. Pages return native public Responses and never contain tenant data.
Bindings and triggers belong in maximus() in vite.config.ts; Env is generated from them. Database migrations
and public asset admission remain explicit; adding files never provisions infrastructure.

## Boundaries

Tenant authority is context.principal.organizationId, never caller input. Declare strict schemas,
scopes, effects and the required transports once. Use the shared Result pipeline. Never put provider
credentials, customer data or request bodies in logs, examples, errors or agent instructions.
Secrets belong in bindings; .dev.vars is local and ignored. Production tokens are refused until the
application configures a real identity provider or cryptographically verified resolver.

## Workflows

Use `bun run verify` for type generation, TypeScript, lint, format and build. Tests require an explicit
human request, including tests in scripts, hooks or CI. Never start them implicitly.
Use `cf` for Cloudflare; discover account/resource commands with anonymous `cf cli search` queries
and inspect their schema before execution. Deploy with the project's script or its GitHub workflow.
Preserve unrelated work and Git identity configuration. Do not add assistant attribution to commits.

Vite+ owns the root toolchain: `vite.config.ts` configures lint/format, `vp check` checks them,
`vp build` bundles the Worker and `vp dev` runs it locally. TypeScript and Cloudflare type generation
remain part of `bun run verify`. Tests are never part of automatic deployment.
